{
	"title": "Loi binomiale et loi de Bernoulli : espérance, variance, écart type",
	"description": "E(X) = np, V(X) = np(1 − p), σ(X) = √(np(1 − p)) ; Bernoulli : V = p(1 − p) ; nombre moyen de succès (pièges : np(1 − p) contre np, variance contre écart type)",
	"grades": ["T_SPE", "T_COMP"],
	"points": ["TCOMP-089", "TCOMP-085", "TCOMP-098", "TSPE-245", "TSPE-225", "TSPE-249"],
	"theme": "Probabilités",
	"domain": "Loi binomiale",
	"subdomain": "Espérance et variance",
	"level": 1,
	"status": "draft",
	"delay": 60,
	"shared": {
		"blankDefaults": {
			"acceptDecimal": true
		}
	},
	"variations": [
		{
			"statement": "La variable aléatoire $X$ suit la loi binomiale $\\mathcal{B}\\left({{n}}\\,;{{eval:t/100;d}}\\right)$.\n\nCalcule son espérance (nombre entier ou décimal).\n\n$E(X)=?$",
			"variables": [
				{
					"name": "n",
					"expression": "20|40|50|60|80|100|150|200"
				},
				{
					"name": "t",
					"expression": "1..40"
				}
			],
			"blanks": [
				{
					"expectedAnswer": "{{eval:n*t/100}}"
				}
			],
			"correction": {
				"steps": [
					"Pour $X\\sim\\mathcal{B}(n\\,;p)$ : $E(X)=np$.",
					"$E(X)={{n}}\\times{{eval:t/100;d}}=\\textcolor{{{color:primary.0}}}{{{eval:n*t/100;d}}}$."
				]
			}
		},
		{
			"statement": "La variable aléatoire $X$ suit la loi binomiale $\\mathcal{B}\\left({{n}}\\,;{{eval:t/10;d}}\\right)$.\n\nCalcule sa variance (nombre entier ou décimal).\n\n$V(X)=?$",
			"variables": [
				{
					"name": "n",
					"expression": "10|20|30|50|100"
				},
				{
					"name": "t",
					"expression": "1..9"
				}
			],
			"blanks": [
				{
					"expectedAnswer": "{{eval:n*t*(10-t)/100}}"
				}
			],
			"correction": {
				"steps": [
					"Pour $X\\sim\\mathcal{B}(n\\,;p)$ : $V(X)=np(1-p)$.",
					"$V(X)={{n}}\\times{{eval:t/10;d}}\\times{{eval:1-t/10;d}}=\\textcolor{{{color:primary.0}}}{{{eval:n*t*(10-t)/100;d}}}$."
				]
			}
		},
		{
			"statement": "La variable aléatoire $X$ suit la loi binomiale $\\mathcal{B}\\left({{n}}\\,;{{p}}\\right)$.\n\nCalcule son écart type $\\sigma(X)$ (valeur exacte).\n\n$\\sigma(X)=?$",
			"variables": [
				{
					"name": "w",
					"expression": "1..8"
				},
				{
					"name": "n",
					"expression": "{{if:w==1|16|{{if:w==2|36|{{if:w==3|64|{{if:w==4|100|{{if:w==5|25|{{if:w==6|100|{{if:w==7|100|400}}}}}}}}}}}}}}"
				},
				{
					"name": "pp",
					"expression": "{{if:w==1|0.5|{{if:w==2|0.5|{{if:w==3|0.5|{{if:w==4|0.5|{{if:w==5|0.2|{{if:w==6|0.2|{{if:w==7|0.1|0.1}}}}}}}}}}}}}}"
				},
				{
					"name": "p",
					"expression": "{{eval:pp;d}}"
				},
				{
					"name": "s",
					"expression": "{{if:w==1|2|{{if:w==2|3|{{if:w==3|4|{{if:w==4|5|{{if:w==5|2|{{if:w==6|4|{{if:w==7|3|6}}}}}}}}}}}}}}"
				}
			],
			"blanks": [
				{
					"expectedAnswer": "{{s}}"
				}
			],
			"correction": {
				"steps": [
					"$V(X)=np(1-p)={{n}}\\times{{p}}\\times{{eval:1-pp;d}}={{eval:s^2}}$.",
					"$\\sigma(X)=\\sqrt{V(X)}=\\sqrt{ {{eval:s^2}} }=\\textcolor{{{color:primary.0}}}{{{s}}}$."
				]
			}
		},
		{
			"statement": "La variable aléatoire $X$ suit la loi de Bernoulli de paramètre $p=\\dfrac{ {{c}} }{ {{q}} }$.\n\nCalcule sa variance.\n\n$V(X)=?$",
			"variables": [
				{
					"name": "q",
					"expression": "3..8"
				},
				{
					"name": "c",
					"expression": "1..{{eval:q-1}}"
				}
			],
			"conditions": ["gcd(c, q) == 1"],
			"blanks": [
				{
					"expectedAnswer": "{{eval:c*(q-c)/q^2}}"
				}
			],
			"correction": {
				"steps": [
					"Pour une loi de Bernoulli : $E(X)=p$ et $V(X)=p(1-p)$.",
					"$V(X)=\\dfrac{ {{c}} }{ {{q}} }\\times\\dfrac{ {{eval:q-c}} }{ {{q}} }=\\textcolor{{{color:primary.0}}}{{{eval:c*(q-c)/q^2}}}$."
				]
			}
		},
		{
			"statement": "Un questionnaire comporte ${{n}}$ questions ; pour chacune, ${{q}}$ réponses sont proposées, dont une seule est juste. Un élève répond au hasard à chaque question, indépendamment.\n\nCombien de bonnes réponses peut-il espérer en moyenne ?\n\n$?$",
			"variables": [
				{
					"name": "n",
					"expression": "10|12|15|20|24|30|40"
				},
				{
					"name": "q",
					"expression": "2..5"
				}
			],
			"blanks": [
				{
					"expectedAnswer": "{{eval:n/q}}"
				}
			],
			"correction": {
				"steps": [
					"Le nombre $X$ de bonnes réponses suit la loi $\\mathcal{B}\\left({{n}}\\,;\\dfrac{1}{ {{q}} }\\right)$.",
					"$E(X)=np={{n}}\\times\\dfrac{1}{ {{q}} }=\\textcolor{{{color:primary.0}}}{{{eval:n/q}}}$ bonnes réponses en moyenne."
				]
			}
		}
	],
